(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[12 1 "// compile()'s PyCF_ONLY_AST (PY6h's REQUEST, queue 200; ast.parse, ast.literal_eval): the host parses (the compiler's"] [13 1 "// mode \"ast:MODE:FLAGS:FEATURE:OPTIMIZE\"; since PY9, queue 201, the native reader, arbace.repr.python.astjson, in"] [14 1 "// tools/pyi/ast_json.py's form) and answers the tree as JSON; here it is rebuilt as the _ast module's nodes. A compile()"] [15 1 "// of an AST object is converted and validated first (queue 202c, builtins_ast_validate.go), then unparses it"] [16 1 "// (ast.unparse) and compiles the text: its positions are the unparsed text's."] [18 1 "// parseAST is the tree of source as _ast nodes."] [27 2 "// the compiler's answer for a SyntaxError (PY9: the native reader's, IndentationError and TabError too, the text"] [28 2 "// the parser's)"] [52 3 "// a tree nested past encoding/json's depth (10,000; py-os-1124, test_pyrepl's test_runsource_compile_error: '-' *"] [53 3 "// 100_000 + '1'): the parser's MemoryError, as pegen's MAXSTACK raises it on such a source"] [67 2 "// optimize > 0 or 2 (queue 202c): the tree preprocessed as ast_preprocess.c does (builtins_ast_opt.go)"] [137 1 "// astIntLiteralLimit is the parser's int digits limit (_PyPegen_number_token: PyLong_FromString's ValueError for a"] [138 1 "// decimal literal of more than sys.get_int_max_str_digits() digits, a SyntaxError of the literal's line, columns"] [139 1 "// 0). The host's parser does not know the runtime's limit and its answer gives the value in decimal, so the literal's"] [140 1 "// radix is read from the source at the node's position: a decimal literal has as many digits as its value, less"] [141 1 "// its underscores (queue 211: test_ast's test_literal_eval_str_int_limit)."] [174 1 "// astIdentifierKey is whether a field's values are identifiers (or lists of them), interned as the parser's"] [175 1 "// _PyPegen_new_identifier interns them (queue 202c: node.id is 'x')."] [246 14 "// a str with a lone surrogate (queue 232): its UTF-16 units, pairs combined (load.go's codepoints)"] [265 1 "// unparseAST is ast.unparse(tree), for compile() of an AST object."] [271 2 "// __import__(\"ast\") is the package's top: ast itself"] [287 1 "// isASTNode is o an instance of _ast.AST."] [301 1 "// compile() of an AST object (queue 202c; Python/bltinmodule.c's is_ast branch): the object is converted as"] [302 1 "// Python-ast.c's obj2ast_* functions convert it (the node's fields and attributes by Parser/Python.asdl, TypeError and"] [303 1 "// ValueError as theirs), then checked by Python/ast.c's _PyAST_Validate. With PyCF_ONLY_AST the tree is preprocessed"] [304 1 "// (Python/ast_preprocess.c: optimize > 0's folding, optimize 2's docstrings) and made objects again as"] [305 1 "// PyAST_mod2obj makes them; else it is unparsed and the text compiled (PY6h's design)."] [307 1 "// astField is a field or an attribute of Python.asdl: its name, its type and its quantifier (\"\", \"?\", \"*\")."] [310 1 "// astCon is a constructor of a sum (sum its sum's name) or a product type (sum \"\")."] [317 1 "// astSum is a sum type: its attributes and constructors; simple when no constructor has a field."] [327 27 "// constructors of sums and products, by name"] [328 27 "// the _ast module's classes, by name"] [341 1 "// astSchemaOf is the schema of astTable with the module's classes (the module imported first)."] [383 1 "// astNode is a node of the C level's tree: its constructor's (or product's) name and its fields' values: nil (NULL),"] [384 1 "// *astNode, []any (a sequence), Object (identifier, string, constant) or int; pos its attributes when it has some."] [422 1 "// obj2ast converts obj, a value of the asdl type typ (obj2ast_TYPE)."] [484 1 "// field converts the field f of obj for owner (the node's name in the messages)."] [529 1 "// attrs reads the position attributes (the optional ends default to the starts)."] [558 1 "// fields reads a constructor's fields, then checks its required ones as the C constructor (_PyAST_NAME) does."] [638 1 "// astObj2Mod is PyAST_obj2mod: the mode's node checked (PyAst_CheckMode), then converted."] [660 1 "// ---- Python/ast.c: _PyAST_Validate ----"] [1403 1 "// astValidate is _PyAST_Validate."] [1420 1 "// ---- PyAST_mod2obj ----"] [1422 1 "// ast2obj makes x, a value of the asdl type typ, objects again (ast2obj_TYPE): a node of the _ast module's class with"] [1423 1 "// every field and attribute set."] [1465 1 "// compileASTObject is compile()'s branch for an AST object: with PyCF_ONLY_AST the converted, validated and"] [1466 1 "// preprocessed tree as objects; else the validated tree's text (ast.unparse) for the compiler."] [1482 2 "// an identifier that is no Python identifier (queue 232): CPython compiles the tree's names as given, any str (pytest's"] [1483 2 "// assertion rewriting names its temporaries @py_assert1, @py_builtins, @pytest_ar), where the unparsed text would be a"] [1484 2 "// syntax error: each such name respelled (astRespell) in a copy of the tree, the same str the same spelling, the"] [1485 2 "// copy unparsed, and the respellings returned (spelling to name) for unrespellCode to put the names back into the"] [1486 2 "// compiled code (pytest's mark expressions evaluate $-prefixed names against a mapping that sees them)"] [1506 1 "// unrespellCode puts the names respellIdents respelled back into code compiled from the respelled text: its name,"] [1507 1 "// qualified name, locals, cells, frees and names, its str constants (keyword names among them) and its nested code,"] [1508 1 "// the names' interned Strs made again."] [1555 1 "// astRespell is a name's spelling as a Python identifier, unique to it: \"_pyi_\" then each character that is a"] [1556 1 "// letter, digit or \"_\" as it is, any other as \"_xHH_\" (its code point in hex), so that no two strs meet."] [1573 1 "// respellIdents respells, in place, each identifier field of the converted tree n that is no Python identifier"] [1574 1 "// (astRespell, names the spellings given); true when one was."] [1591 5 "// an import's module names are dotted: alias.name, ImportFrom.module"] [1642 1 "// The AST's preprocessing (queue 202c; Python/ast_preprocess.c, _PyAST_Preprocess, as compile() runs it for"] [1643 1 "// PyCF_ONLY_AST): with PyCF_OPTIMIZED_AST (ast.parse's optimize > 0) the folding: __debug__ a constant, a str's %"] [1644 1 "// formatting with a tuple a JoinedStr, a pattern's negative and complex numbers constants; with optimize 2 the"] [1645 1 "// docstrings removed. Without PyCF_OPTIMIZED_AST (syntax_check_only) only the docstrings at optimize 2."] [1655 1 "// astNeedsPreprocess is whether the preprocessing can change a tree."] [1660 1 "// astPreprocess is _PyCompile_AstPreprocess (its future features from the tree, _PyFuture_FromAST)."] [1681 1 "// astFutureAnnotations is `from __future__ import annotations` among the module's leading statements (future.c)."] [1709 1 "// astDocString is _PyAST_GetDocString: the body's first statement's str constant."] [1945 1 "// astMakeConst makes e the constant v (make_const), its position kept."] [1970 1 "// astOptimizeFormat is optimize_format: '%s %r' % (a, b) as an f-string, when every unit is a simple s, r or a."] [1975 3 "// parse_literal"] [2016 1 "// astParseFormat is parse_format with simple_format_arg_parse (at most two digits of width and of precision)."] [2102 1 "// foldMatchConst is fold_const_match_patterns: -C and C1 +/- C2 of a pattern's value made constants."]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[42 33] [51 26] [72 53] [103 32] [108 49] [147 30] [165 32] [190 24] [199 52] [249 13] [249 29] [252 52] [413 23] [416 47] [453 28] [467 27] [470 25] [506 13] [506 20] [511 31] [541 22] [571 31] [597 48] [607 44] [627 44] [697 46] [700 43] [703 49] [712 55] [722 28] [725 33] [726 33] [735 40] [738 33] [741 27] [742 50] [746 39] [749 26] [750 50] [760 53] [784 37] [794 23] [801 27] [812 42] [816 25] [826 24] [827 32] [845 40] [855 49] [862 49] 